list.item:
 Carter, James E., Governor of Georgia;
President-Elect from November 1976 to January 19, 1977; President of the
United States from January 20, 1977 to January 20, 1981

 Hartman, Arthur A., Assistant Secretary of State
for European and Canadian Affairs from January 8, 1974 to June 8,
1977

 Robinson, Charles W., Under Secretary of State
for Economic and Agricultural Affairs from January 3, 1975 to April 9, 1976;
Deputy Secretary of State from 1976 to January 1977

person.note:
Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs until February 1, 1973;
                    Ambassador at Large from February 2, 1973 to February 28, 1977; National
                    Security Council Under Secretaries Committee, 1973

Director, Office of Management and Budget from June 1970 to May 1972;
                    Secretary of the Treasury from June 12, 1972 to May 8, 1974; Member of the
                    President’s Foreign Intelligence Advisory Board

Executive Secretary of the Department from January 31, 1974 to July 14, 1976;
                    Director of the Foreign Service Institute from July 14, 1976 to February 29,
                    1980
